1. Relations at l. For any finite free O-submodule Z of functions
Gamma -> O^n, take F=O^(Gamma x {1,...,n}) with finite support and the
evaluation map e:F->Z^*, e(e_(g,j))(z)=z(g)_j. A B-valued vector function
is a linear functional F->B. If it obeys all matrix-valued relations of
Z, it kills ker(e): put any scalar relation in just one fixed row of a
matrix relation, possible since n>=1. Conversely each matrix row is a
scalar relation. Thus the obeying functions identify with
Hom_O(im(e),B). The image is a submodule of the finite free dual Z^*,
so is finite free of rank <= rank Z (DVR). Therefore its length is at
most rank(Z)*b. No surjectivity of e onto Z^*, no reduction-surjectivity
of crystalline cocycles, no saturation assumption on Z is needed.
This is precisely the native length_obeying_relationsOn_le argument.
At v|l set Z=Z_f(L_v), the integral crystalline cocycles of the actual
local matrix lattice from inClass_of_isLatticeIn. Every local restriction
of a global cocycle obeying crysRels(u) obeys all relations of Z, by
obeying_crysRels. Consequently length localCocycles <= rank Z*b, using
the actual placeOver representative (hence bounds the infimum over A).
Keep the potentially crystalline finite generation and rank theorem as
explicit prerequisites; do not identify torsion crystalline with reductions.

