3. Sum the crystalline ranks before estimating. For each v|l the native
rank formula is rank Z_f(L_v)=n+sum_{sigma in E_v} neg(J_sigma),
where E_v consists of the complex embeddings read by localChart at v.
These embedding sets are disjoint across v: a common embedding would
induce the same l-adic place. Thus their total negative count is at
most sum_sigma neg(J_sigma). By IsRowType.card_neg_le,
neg(J_sigma)+neg(J_star_sigma)<=n. Conjugation permutes the embeddings;
there are 2f embeddings. Therefore 2 sum_sigma neg(J_sigma)<=2fn.
It follows that sum_{v|l} rank Z_f(L_v) <= (|S_l|+f)n.
Combining with step 2, for every a dividing l^M on the SAME lattice,
  sum_{v in S} inf_A length localCocycles(u,crysRels u,A,B)
  <= (|S|+f)n*b + sum_{v in S_g} addVal_O det(u(gamma_v)-1).
The infimum is bounded above by the particular placeOver used in the
proof. This is the exact coefficient (|S|+f)*length B^n required by
IsBalanced.local_length_le, not a 2n-per-place estimate.

4. Add the mirror cost. Set k=t-1 in Nat (t=0 is read as 1), chi=cycChar.
The native scalar g satisfies u(g)=alpha I, chi(g)=D.g_i^n.
Trace self-duality gives for every h=conjGal(j):
 tr(u(h)u((conjGal g)^-1))
 = chi(j*g^-1)^(-k) tr(u(g*j^-1))
 = chi(g)^k alpha tr(u(h)).
Full integral matrix span and perfect trace pairing on matrix units
force u((conjGal g)^-1)=alpha' I with alpha'=chi(g)^k alpha.
Since alpha is a unit and chi(conjGal g)=chi(g), the required discrepancy
has valuation
  addVal(alpha-chi(conjGal g)*alpha')
  = addVal(1-D.g_i^(n*(k+1))).
Do not replace k+1 by t if t=0. The native exponent is positive and
bounded using n<=D.r, t<=D.t and D.t positive. Its normalized valuation
is <= crudeUnit by ellVal_le_crudeUnit at this exact exponent.
Choose beta=sum_{v in S_g} addVal det(u(gamma_v)-1)
             + n*addVal(alpha-chi(conjGal g)*alpha').
